Description: FactoryTalk Services Platform (FTSP), FactoryTalk Activation Manager, FactoryTalk Linx (data server), FactoryTalk Historian SE, FactoryTalk Batch, and FactoryTalk ViewPoint (IIS web add-on) logs and configuration. This is the umbrella target for non-View FactoryTalk services that share the same host as an FT View SE server. Bulletproof against locked files via AlwaysAddToQueue on critical services.
Author: Raul B Netto (Cybolt DFIR)
Version: 1.1
Id: a6e41e26-b4de-41dd-8e16-ea7f465f9d70
RecreateDirectories: true
Targets:
    -
        Name: FactoryTalk Activation Manager logs
        Category: Logs
        Path: C:\ProgramData\Rockwell\Activation\
        Recursive: true
        FileMask: "*"
        AlwaysAddToQueue: true
        Comment: "Activation Manager logs. CVE-2026-16675 (Sep 2026) LPE. AlwaysAddToQueue: locked by Activation Service at runtime."
    -
        Name: FactoryTalk Activation install dir
        Category: Logs
        Path: C:\Program Files (x86)\Rockwell Software\Activation\
        Recursive: true
        FileMask: "*.log"
        AlwaysAddToQueue: true
        Comment: "Activation Manager installer/runtime logs in Program Files. Locked while service runs."
    -
        Name: FactoryTalk Activation install dir - all
        Category: FileSystem
        Path: C:\Program Files (x86)\Rockwell Software\Activation\
        Recursive: true
        FileMask: "*"
        Comment: "Catch-all: any non-.log file in Activation install (config, ini). NOT AlwaysAddToQueue to keep pass fast."
    -
        Name: FactoryTalk Services Platform install dir - logs
        Category: Logs
        Path: C:\Program Files (x86)\Rockwell Software\FactoryTalk\
        Recursive: true
        FileMask: "*.log"
        AlwaysAddToQueue: true
        Comment: "FTSP runtime logs. Includes FactoryTalk Directory, Security, and Policy Manager services. Locked while services run."
    -
        Name: FactoryTalk Services Platform install dir - all
        Category: FileSystem
        Path: C:\Program Files (x86)\Rockwell Software\FactoryTalk\
        Recursive: true
        FileMask: "*"
        Comment: "Catch-all: any non-.log file in FTSP install. NOT AlwaysAddToQueue."
    -
        Name: FactoryTalk Linx (data server) - logs
        Category: Logs
        Path: C:\Program Files (x86)\Rockwell Software\FactoryTalk Linx\
        Recursive: true
        FileMask: "*.log"
        AlwaysAddToQueue: true
        Comment: "FT Linx / RSLinx-class data server. CIP/EtherNet/IP comms to ControlLogix/CompactLogix live here. Locked while service runs. Critical for PLC comms evidence."
    -
        Name: FactoryTalk Linx (data server) - all
        Category: FileSystem
        Path: C:\Program Files (x86)\Rockwell Software\FactoryTalk Linx\
        Recursive: true
        FileMask: "*"
        Comment: "Catch-all: non-.log files in FT Linx install. NOT AlwaysAddToQueue."
    -
        Name: FactoryTalk Historian SE install dir
        Category: FileSystem
        Path: C:\Program Files\Rockwell Software\FactoryTalk Historian\
        Recursive: true
        FileMask: "*"
        AlwaysAddToQueue: true
        Comment: "FT Historian SE. PIGetMsg.exe lives in Server\\adm\\ for log access. CVE-2025-13036/44019/36539 (login race condition). AlwaysAddToQueue: Historian data store is heavily locked."
    -
        Name: FactoryTalk Batch Event Journal (default)
        Category: FileSystem
        Path: C:\Users\Public\Public Documents\Rockwell Automation\Batch\
        Recursive: true
        FileMask: "*"
        AlwaysAddToQueue: true
        Comment: "Default FT Batch Event Journal path. Batchsvr.ini ErrorLogDirectory may override. AlwaysAddToQueue: journal is constantly appended to."
    -
        Name: FactoryTalk Batch alt install path
        Category: FileSystem
        Path: C:\ProgramData\Rockwell Automation\Batch\
        Recursive: true
        FileMask: "*"
        AlwaysAddToQueue: true
        Comment: "Alternate FT Batch install on modern hosts."
    -
        Name: FactoryTalk ViewPoint install (IIS-backed)
        Category: FileSystem
        Path: C:\inetpub\wwwroot\
        Recursive: true
        FileMask: "*ViewPoint*"
        Comment: "FT ViewPoint web application root. Pair with IISLogFiles target for full web traffic (CVE-2025-9066 XXE). NOT AlwaysAddToQueue: static web app files."
    -
        Name: Rockwell Software install root - INI files
        Category: FileSystem
        Path: C:\Program Files (x86)\Rockwell Software\
        Recursive: true
        FileMask: "*.ini"
        Comment: "All Rockwell .ini config files for installed services. Fast triage of which FTSP components are present and how they are configured."
    -
        Name: Rockwell Software install root - all configs
        Category: FileSystem
        Path: C:\Program Files (x86)\Rockwell Software\
        Recursive: true
        FileMask: "*.config"
        Comment: ".NET config files (.config) for Rockwell services. Tells us service config, connection strings, etc."

# Documentation
# The path C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Rockwell Software\\ is the canonical install
# root for the entire FactoryTalk suite on x64 Windows. Listing this directory
# is a quick way to enumerate which components are installed. The 32-bit path
# applies even on x64 Windows because most FactoryTalk services are still
# 32-bit or installer-32-bit-on-64.
#
# Bulletproof notes:
#   - All .log captures have AlwaysAddToQueue: true because the corresponding
#     service has these files open at runtime. Raw read is necessary if we
#     triage a live host.
#   - The catch-all duplicates WITHOUT AlwaysAddToQueue cover config files and
#     other artifacts that aren't actively locked.
#
# Cross-references:
#   - Activation: CVE-2026-16675
#   - Historian SE: CVE-2025-13036 / 44019 / 36539
#   - ViewPoint: CVE-2025-9066
#   - View SE: CVE-2024-45824, CVE-2024-7513
#   - View ME: CVE-2025-24479, CVE-2025-24480, CVE-2025-9063/9064
